tify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Fred+Neil+Faretheewell+%28Fred%27s+Tune%29", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/song/1488044743", "search": false}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Fred+Neil+Faretheewell+%28Fred%27s+Tune%29", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Fred+Neil+Faretheewell+%28Fred%27s+Tune%29&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["1966 Capitol Records"]}, {"t": 6929, "time": "01:55:29", "artist": "Jackson C. Frank", "title": "Juliette (1972)", "conf": "high", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Jackson+C.+Frank+Juliette+%281972%29", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Jackson+C.+Frank+Juliette+%281972%29", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Jackson+C.+Frank+Juliette+%281972%29", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Jackson+C.+Frank+Juliette+%281972%29", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/song/1136643390", "search": false}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Jackson+C.+Frank+Juliette+%281972%29", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Jackson+C.+Frank+Juliette+%281972%29&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["2015 Secret Records"]}], "counts": {"high": 6, "mid": 8, "low": 7}, "transcripts": [{"start": "00:10:19", "end": "00:10:57", "text": "Good evening. Sam here, producer of M5. Lucky enough to cover tonight, thank you to Lilly. Firstly, I'd like to acknowledge the Gadigal people of the Uyura Nation on which FBi broadcast on, paying respects to Elders both past, present and emerging. It's been a while since I've done a cover, I think four months I think, so I'm super excited to play some music. if you want to send some love any questions, have a chat you can message in on 0435 123 945"}, {"start": "00:20:35", "end": "00:20:50", "text": "I'm listening to Terry Callia, Cotton Eye Joe, made in 1965, not to be confused with the Rednecks, Cotton Eye Joe."}, {"start": "00:46:44", "end": "00:47:23", "text": "Just checking in. Last few songs you've been listening to. A couple songs ago was by Savannah Silver Band. Like I Do. It's from Melbourne in the late 1970s. We're listening now to The Soul of Love by Peter Goblin. And in between those two songs was Fantasy Woman by Lauren Cornelius. text in give me some company on 0435 123 945 I'd love to hear from you"}, {"start": "01:19:00", "end": "01:19:22", "text": "I hope we're all enjoying ourselves at the moment. We're listening to White Nile by Kellen, Phil, Corrin and Legacy, released last year on their album African Skies. And what we listened to beforehand was Matthew Halsall's Together, released in 2009."}, {"start": "01:37:39", "end": "01:38:01", "text": "Pharoah Sanders' song. It's Kazuko, the instrumental. And what we were listening to before was the Australian Art Orchestra with Nunguyu, Nunguyu. Not long to go now, about 20 minutes. And then we'll hand you over to the all-nighters. Hope you've been enjoying the music. Rest in peace."}, {"start": "01:58:44", "end": "01:59:02", "text": "Alrighty, this will be my last song. It's been a pleasure. This is Jackson F. Frank with Juliet. It's been good to be back on the radio and share some music with you all. We'll see you next time."}], "fbi_json": [{"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:03:00"}, "track": {"title": "Serpentskirt", "artists": [{"name": "Cocteau Twins"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "low"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:04:14"}, "track": {"title": "Eternal Caravan of Reincarnation", "artists": [{"name": "Santana"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:11:00"}, "track": {"title": "Cosmic Voltage", "artists": [{"name": "68mafi